Files in this repository derived from, or whose protocol/data-model knowledge originates from,
ElevenHack's reverse-engineering work:

- Source/Rack/SysExFrame.h, Source/Rack/SysExFrame.cpp
  (from ElevenHack's gs.elevenhack.midi.SysEx)
- Source/Rack/SevenBitCodec.h, Source/Rack/SevenBitCodec.cpp
  (from ElevenHack's gs.elevenhack.midi.SysEx and gs.elevenhack.ParseUtils)
- Source/Rack/EffectDefinitions.h, Source/Rack/EffectDefinitions.cpp
  (from ElevenHack's gs.elevenhack.ER.Effect and gs.elevenhack.ER.EffectAmpCab)

These are original C++ implementations - not line-by-line ports - independently structured and
tested against real Eleven Rack hardware captures (see docs/protocol-spec.md). The underlying
protocol knowledge they encode (SysEx message format, command IDs, effect/parameter mappings)
originates from ElevenHack, which was itself developed without official AVID documentation.
